on  to the ordinary Muslim community  referring to the recent violence the UN  Special Rapporteur says Sri Lanka's  government must do more to protect  minorities in order to challenge  extremism and create inclusion you  really need to have you know rule of law  well protector well rule of law is not  protected then then the weaker  communities are vulnerable to attacks  and the majority feels they can exploit  that space to the up to the advantage  Shaheed says reforming the education  system to teach respect for all  religions is important Shaheed says Sri  Lankans should work towards creating a  common identity beyond religion and race  given the country's violent past more  Sri Lankans are likely to agree if  politicians will let them win a  Fernandez al Jazeera Colombo
 

